{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733882",
      "title": "Understanding Relative & Absolute Paths",
      "sourceHash": "c63d9bfc8bcbdf4dd917a51684ae579f913ca7185337021b99cbaf06f9355853",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "Now to conclude",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "this basics part about React Routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 10.38,
          "en": "I wanna talk about paths again, which might sound boring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "but which is important to understand and get right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 16.05,
          "en": "When defining our routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.05,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "we define the paths for which they should be active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 22.92,
          "en": "We got this root wrapper route, here, and then we got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 25.473,
          "en": "a couple of child routes inside of that route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "Now actually, all the paths I'm defining here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 34.01,
          "en": "are absolute paths because they all start with a slash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 35.13,
          "en": "This simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.13,
          "end": 39.15,
          "en": "that they're always seen from after the domain name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.15,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "Now, this is an important detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 45.87,
          "en": "If I would, for example, changed this wrapper path to /root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "you will notice that if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 50.613,
          "en": "for /products, I don't see anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 55.743,
          "en": "but neither do I for /root/products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.61,
          "end": 58.68,
          "en": "If I type in just /root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.68,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "I also don't see anything on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "And the reason for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 64.89,
          "en": "is that if I open my developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.89,
          "end": 68.88,
          "en": "I got an error that I got the absolute route path slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 71.373,
          "en": "nested under path /root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 75.45,
          "en": "So the problem I'm having here is that, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "we have absolute paths here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "because they're starting with a slash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "that's how you can tell that these are absolute paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 87.42,
          "en": "If a path starts with a slash, it is an absolute path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.42,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "And we now have clashing route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 92.67,
          "en": "We're saying that the parent route, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.67,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "should handle all pages that start with /root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "but then the child pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 101.946,
          "en": "actually don't start with /root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.946,
          "end": 104.16,
          "en": "Now of course, here it doesn't make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.16,
          "end": 106.14,
          "en": "to start with /root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.14,
          "end": 108.36,
          "en": "but it's important to understand the problem here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.36,
          "end": 110.78999999999999,
          "en": "and the difference between absolute paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "as we have them here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 116.25,
          "en": "and relative paths because that's the alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.25,
          "end": 120.36,
          "en": "We can remove those leading slashes here on the child routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.36,
          "end": 123.42,
          "en": "and that turns these route definition paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.42,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "to relative paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 128.64,
          "en": "So now we got three relative paths here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "instead of absolute paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "Now, when defining routes like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "this simply means that these paths defined here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "are appended after the path of the wrapper route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 143.64,
          "en": "So if we have a child route with a relative path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.64,
          "end": 145.98,
          "en": "then React Router will take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.98,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "at the path of the parent route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 151.983,
          "en": "and append the child route path after the parent route path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.97,
          "end": 156.45,
          "en": "So if you make those changes, this error goes away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 159.45,
          "en": "and for just /root we see the starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.45,
          "end": 163.5,
          "en": "and for /root/products we see the products page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.5,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "Of course, for just /products, we don't see anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 169.62,
          "en": "Instead we get the default error message, again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.62,
          "end": 172.32,
          "en": "We also don't see the content of our error page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.32,
          "end": 175.74,
          "en": "because now we got this error for some page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.74,
          "end": 179.16,
          "en": "that we tried to find after slash nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 183.06,
          "en": "but this error element is added to the /root path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.06,
          "end": 186.18,
          "en": "therefore it's not activated here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.18,
          "end": 187.08,
          "en": "Now, of course, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.08,
          "end": 190.17,
          "en": "I don't want to have /root as a starting path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.17,
          "end": 192.03,
          "en": "I want to have slash nothing instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.03,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "but we can still stick to relative paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "for these child routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.21,
          "en": "because we wanna append these paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.21,
          "end": 202.05,
          "en": "after the path of the wrapper parent route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.05,
          "end": 205.32,
          "en": "But that is not all you should know about paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.32,
          "end": 208.05,
          "en": "Instead, paths also play an important role",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.05,
          "end": 211.32,
          "en": "if we think about links, like here in the main navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.32,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "or in the products.js file where we also have links.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "Here, we are also defining paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 220.29,
          "en": "and the same rules as before apply.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.29,
          "end": 224.52,
          "en": "If a path starts with a slash, with a leading forward slash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 227.136,
          "en": "then it is an absolute path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.136,
          "end": 232.02,
          "en": "So clicking that link will always visit /products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.02,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "Again, you can see the problem if I do switch back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 238.92000000000002,
          "en": "to /root, here, for my root route temporarily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.92000000000002,
          "end": 240.75,
          "en": "in my route definitions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 245.34,
          "en": "and I then go to /root/products, this works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.34,
          "end": 248.43,
          "en": "but if I click one of these links here, we get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 252.66,
          "en": "because those links leads to /products/p1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.66,
          "end": 253.493,
          "en": "Why?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.493,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "Because in the products.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 257.82,
          "en": "that is the path we defined here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.82,
          "end": 260.13,
          "en": "and since it starts with a forward slash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.13,
          "end": 261.48,
          "en": "it's an absolute path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.48,
          "end": 264.6,
          "en": "so it's added directly after the domain name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.6,
          "end": 267.363,
          "en": "not after the currently active path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.47,
          "end": 270.93,
          "en": "But we could switch to the latter behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.93,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "and instead create relative paths here on those links.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 278.7,
          "en": "We could, for example, do that in the home.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.7,
          "end": 281.52,
          "en": "by instead of linking to /products",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.52,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "to change this to just products",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 286.293,
          "en": "without the slash at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 290.58,
          "en": "With that, this is now a relative path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.58,
          "end": 293.4,
          "en": "and this link has a relative path now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.4,
          "end": 296.73,
          "en": "which means that, by default, it will add this path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 296.73,
          "end": 299.673,
          "en": "after the currently active routes path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 300.72,
          "end": 303.87,
          "en": "So if we go back to just /root",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 306,
          "en": "and I click the list of products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306,
          "end": 307.86,
          "en": "which is that link I just edited,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 307.86,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "you see it'll lead me to /root/products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 313.29,
          "en": "And, previously, it would've failed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 313.29,
          "end": 315.78,
          "en": "as you can see here in the main navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 315.78,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "where we have absolute paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 319.83299999999997,
          "en": "to routes that we no longer support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 320.67,
          "end": 324.18,
          "en": "And in products.js, we can also switch to a relative path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 324.18,
          "end": 327.66,
          "en": "by simply removing that /products/ part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 327.66,
          "end": 329.64,
          "en": "Now we just add the product ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 329.64,
          "end": 332.19,
          "en": "after the currently actives route path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 332.19,
          "end": 334.59000000000003,
          "en": "and that, of course, means we can also get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 334.59000000000003,
          "end": 337.8,
          "en": "of this entire template literal part here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 337.8,
          "end": 340.74,
          "en": "and just change the path to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 340.74,
          "end": 343.86,
          "en": "And with that, it's added after the currently active path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 343.86,
          "end": 346.89,
          "en": "and therefore these links work again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 346.89,
          "end": 349.65,
          "en": "So it's really important to understand these differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 349.65,
          "end": 353.043,
          "en": "between relative and absolute paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 354,
          "end": 355.86,
          "en": "And when using the link component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 355.86,
          "end": 358.17,
          "en": "you also have a special relative prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 358.17,
          "end": 359.58,
          "en": "which you can add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 359.58,
          "end": 363.15,
          "en": "And this can be set to one of two values, at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 363.15,
          "end": 365.52,
          "en": "to path or route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 365.52,
          "end": 369.39,
          "en": "With that you control whether this segment here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 369.39,
          "end": 372.78,
          "en": "is added relative to the currently actives route path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 372.78,
          "end": 375.93,
          "en": "or to the currently active path in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 375.93,
          "end": 377.97,
          "en": "And that might sometimes be the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 377.97,
          "end": 380.34,
          "en": "but sometimes it's also not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 380.34,
          "end": 381.96,
          "en": "To show you the difference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.96,
          "end": 384.78,
          "en": "let me go back to my route definitions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 384.78,
          "end": 388.29,
          "en": "And there, please note that this route definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 388.29,
          "end": 390.63,
          "en": "which is responsible for the product details,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 390.63,
          "end": 392.76,
          "en": "is a direct child of this root route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 392.76,
          "end": 395.76,
          "en": "not of this products route, but of this root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 395.76,
